{"base_rate":0.3556430446194226,"brier":0.11800669291338582,"bss":0.48504912634055064,"bss_hi":0.5577994265695868,"bss_lo":0.3994426644131986,"chart":{"base":[523.2,105.0],"fp":[267.2,314.0],"lead":"62,268.5 272,237.2 482,187.2 692,95.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.49 — higher than 87% of cities","fp":"low end +7pp, high end +8pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 81% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 4%; promised 97% → rained 89%"},"rel":"62,448.9 129,372.2 452.9,215.9 676.2,81.4"},"country":"DE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.06586614173228347,"ess":423.1426861996236,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Berlin</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Berlin rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (97%), believe about\n<b>89%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nBERLIN-TEMPELHOF, 6.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.49, ranked 17 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(8&ndash;40) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>303</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>31%</b></td><td class='num'>84</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'><b>47%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>79%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>155</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Berlin</b> <span class=\"muted\">DE</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.49</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>8&ndash;40\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Berlin &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Berlin\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 71.11882352941176,349.88235294117646 115.48285714285714,295.33333333333337 221.5661538461539,172.00000000000003 336.79891891891896,62.27027027027026 403.1157419354839,20.348387096774218 403.1157419354839,36.78709677419357 336.79891891891896,131.13513513513516 221.5661538461539,251.33333333333334 115.48285714285714,351.6666666666667 71.11882352941176,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"252.54593175853017\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"252.54593175853017\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,367.58415841584156 71.11882352941176,344.52941176470586 115.48285714285714,269.3333333333333 221.5661538461539,209.33333333333334 336.79891891891896,131.13513513513516 403.1157419354839,57.92258064516125\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 303 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"367.58415841584156\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"71.11882352941176\" cy=\"344.52941176470586\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 31% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 84 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"115.48285714285714\" cy=\"269.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 46%&amp;#10;It rained 47% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"221.5661538461539\" cy=\"209.33333333333334\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 79%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"336.79891891891896\" cy=\"131.13513513513516\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 155 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"403.1157419354839\" cy=\"57.92258064516125\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(36%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Berlin the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.58) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.41).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.412</td><td class='num'>9.5%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>0.431</td><td class='num'>8.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.446</td><td class='num'>5.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.584</td><td class='num'>6.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":52.52437,"lon":13.41053,"n":762,"n_cities":134,"name":"Berlin","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":303,"obs":0.039603960396039604,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.037058823529411755,"n":68,"obs":0.10294117647058823,"sig":true},{"hi":0.3,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.16238095238095238,"n":84,"obs":0.30952380952